      "description": "Code to build",
      "narrationSegment": "A CI/CD pipeline begins when a developer pushes code to a feature branch and opens a pull request. GitHub Actions triggers the CI pipeline: it checks out the code, installs dependencies with pnpm, runs ESLint and TypeScript type checks, then executes the full Vitest test suite — all within 3 minutes.",
